                <pb facs="0333" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg227"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-12-18">December 18,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Rockhill reports that he has been informed by the foreign office that,
                    according to the agreement with the Russian minister, the three cities, Kirin,
                    Harbin, Manchuria, will be opened to international residence and trade January
                    14, 1907.)</p>
            </div>
